::MCR_U02_L03_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L03_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.4
Question:
A context uses the inequality 5x <= 15. What is the solution?
{
=A. x <= 3#Correct. Divide both sides by the positive coefficient to get x <= 3.
~B. x >= 3#This reverses the inequality direction. Dividing by a positive number does not reverse it.
~C. x < 15#This does not divide by the coefficient, so the variable is not isolated.
~D. x = 20#This adds the numbers instead of solving the inequality.
}
